      "text": "Residents wait for the high tide to subside as it peaks at noon in Baseco compound in Manila on Tuesday, May 5, 2026.\n\nAccording to researchers, the flooding is driven by a double threat: as the sea rises, the land in Manila is regularly subsiding, with the relative sea level rise in the city among the highest in the world. This causes \"sunny day flooding\" in western coastal districts, where the tide surges through drainage systems even without a drop of rain. | via Jonathan Cellona, ABS-CBN News",
